yment-options","Deployment Options",[236,237,239],"h3",{"id":238},"helm-charts","Helm Charts",[228,241,242,243,247],{},"Production-ready Helm charts are available in ",[244,245,246],"code",{},"deployment\u002Fhelm\u002F"," for deploying:",[249,250,251,259,265],"ul",{},[252,253,254,258],"li",{},[255,256,257],"strong",{},"Kinotic Server"," — The core platform with configurable replicas, resource limits, and ingress",[252,260,261,264],{},[255,262,263],{},"Elasticsearch"," — Search and persistence cluster",[252,266,267,270],{},[255,268,269],{},"Load Generator"," — For performance testing",[236,272,274],{"id":273},"docker-compose-local-development","Docker Compose (Local Development)",[228,276,277,278,281],{},"A Docker Compose configuration in ",[244,279,280],{},"deployment\u002Fdocker-compose\u002F"," provides a complete local development environment including the Kinotic server, Elasticsearch, and supporting services. This is the recommended way to run Kinotic OS during development.",[236,283,285],{"id":284},"kind-kubernetes-in-docker","KinD (Kubernetes in Docker)",[228,287,288,289,292],{},"For testing Kubernetes deployments locally, ",[244,290,291],{},"deployment\u002Fkind\u002F"," provides a KinD setup with Terraform configurations that deploy the full stack into a local Kubernetes cluster.",[236,294,296],{"id":295},"cloud-providers-terraform","Cloud Providers (Terraform)",[228,298,299,300,303],{},"Terraform configurations in ",[244,301,302],{},"deployment\u002Fterraform\u002F"," support deployment to:",[249,305,306,312],{},[252,307,308,311],{},[255,309,310],{},"AWS"," — EC2-based deployment with configurable instance types",[252,313,314,317],{},[255,315,316],{},"Azure"," — VM-based deployment on Azure infrastructure",[319,320,322],"h4",{"id":321},"organization-storage-on-azure","Organization storage on Azure",[228,324,325,328,329,332,333,336,337,340,341,344,345,348,349,352,353,356,357,360,361,365],{},[244,326,327],{},"deployment\u002Fterraform\u002Fazure\u002Fcluster\u002Forg-storage.tf"," creates what every organization's storage\naccount shares: the ",[244,330,331],{},"rg-\u003Cprefix>-org-storage"," resource group the accounts are created in, a\n",[244,334,335],{},"private-endpoints"," subnet in the platform VNet (",[244,338,339],{},"private_endpoint_subnet_cidr"," in\n",[244,342,343],{},"terraform.tfvars","), and the ",[244,346,347],{},"privatelink.blob.core.windows.net"," private DNS zone linked to\nthat VNet. The accounts themselves are created at runtime by kinotic-server, one per\norganization, when the organization is created. ",[244,350,351],{},"keyvault.tf"," grants the\nkinotic-server identity the roles that takes on the resource group (Storage Account\nContributor, Storage Blob Data Contributor, Network Contributor), on the subnet (Network\nContributor, to join it) and on the DNS zone (Private DNS Zone Contributor), and\n",[244,354,355],{},"kinotic.tf"," hands the server the resource ids as\n",[244,358,359],{},"KINOTIC_SYSTEMAPI_ORGANIZATIONSTORAGE_*"," environment variables (see\n",[362,363,157],"a",{"href":364},"\u002Fplatform\u002Fconfiguration#organization-storage",").",[319,367,369],{"id":368},"ui-sites-on-azure","UI sites on Azure",[228,371,372,375,376,379,380,382,383,385,386,389,390,393,394,397],{},[244,373,374],{},"frontdoor.tf"," creates the one Front Door Standard profile and endpoint every published UI is\nserved through, under ",[244,377,378],{},"apps.\u003Czone>",". kinotic-server creates the rest at runtime: per\norganization an origin group, an origin on the organization's storage account and a rule\nset, and per site a custom domain with a managed certificate, a route, and the CNAME and\nvalidation TXT records in the platform's DNS zone. ",[244,381,351],{}," grants the kinotic-server\nidentity CDN Profile Contributor on the profile and DNS Zone Contributor on the zone, and\n",[244,384,355],{}," passes the profile, endpoint and zone as ",[244,387,388],{},"KINOTIC_SYSTEMAPI_UIDEPLOYMENT_*","\nenvironment variables (see ",[362,391,157],{"href":392},"\u002Fplatform\u002Fconfiguration#ui-sites","). The\n",[244,395,396],{},"kinotic-server"," values file for development disables the provisioner instead.",[228,399,400,401,404,405,408,409,413],{},"A developer machine gets the same two pieces from ",[244,402,403],{},"deployment\u002Fterraform\u002Fazure\u002Fdev",": a resource\ngroup for the accounts and a Front Door profile and endpoint under ",[244,406,407],{},"apps-\u003Cenvironment>.\u003Czone>",",\nwith no VNet, so the server there runs with private endpoints disabled. The\n",[362,410,412],{"href":411},"\u002Fplatform\u002Fcontributing#publishing-uis-against-azure","contributing guide"," walks through it.",{"title":415,"searchDepth":416,"depth":416,"links":417},"",2,[418,419],{"id":226,"depth":416,"text":25},{"id":233,"depth":416,"text":234,"children":420},[421,423,424,425],{"id":238,"depth":422,"text":239},3,{"id":273,"depth":422,"text":274},{"id":284,"depth":422,"text":285},{"id":295,"depth":422,"text":296},"Deploying and operating Kinotic OS in various environments.","md",null,{},{"icon":6},{"title":153,"description":426},"B486vBsgoOCFXPXriE3Mi_whuvmW5e1gvTjaon4_iGY",[434,436],{"title":148,"path":149,"stem":150,"description":435,"icon":151,"children":-1},"High-level architecture of the Kinotic OS platform.",{"title":157,"path":158,"stem":159,"description":437,"icon":160,"children":-1},"Configuration reference for Kinotic OS server and services.",1788505373846]